  "prefLabel": "Cor 101.01 Behavioral health treatment team",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Cor 101.01 “Behavioral health treatment team” means the staff members assigned to monitor and assist persons under departmental control in their rehabilitation or treatment, and which includes the individual’s case manager and other professional staff members of the division of medical and forensics services assigned to the bureau of behavioral health.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Cor 100) #7446, eff 2-6-01; ss by #12500, eff 3-23-18 (formerly Cor 101.15) (See Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Cor 100)",
